Washington, D.C. —Yesterday, Congressman Suozzi sent a letter to President Trump thanking him for securing the Israel-Hamas ceasefire and urging him to continue his work and ensure the bodies of the deceased hostages, including two American citizens, are returned to their families. One of those American hostages, Omer Neutra, was a constituent of Suozzi’s. In the letter, Suozzi writes that “as we celebrate this progress, I must emphasize that the remains of two Americans have not been recovered...while their families rejoice in the release of the other hostages, they cannot begin to truly heal until the bodies of their sons are returned.” “The Neutra family asked me to help bring attention to their cause,” said Suozzi. “I will continue to do anything I can to help them, but we really need the President’s continued help.” In a statement, Ronen and Orna Neutra write that “as parents of Captain Omer Neutra, a U.S.- Israeli citizen still held in Gaza, we are deeply grateful for your leadership and commitment to bringing so many hostages home. This week—when Omer should have been celebrating his 24th birthday—we are instead fighting for the chance to bring him back and lay him to rest with the dignity he deserves. We urge you to continue using your influence and determination until every last hostage is returned.” Suozzi also writes that “these two families and their supporters are left questioning whether the continued captivity of their beloved children stems from genuine challenges in locating them or from the fact that they are American citizens.” ### MEDIA PRESS RELEASES IN THE NEWS OP-EDS Washington DC Office 203 Cannon House Office Building Washington, DC 20515 Phone: (202) 225-3335 Glen Cove District Office 51 Glen Street Second Floor Glen Cove, NY 11542 Phone: (516) 861-1070, Monday to Friday 9:00 am to 5:30 pm Douglaston District Office Douglaston District Office 242-09 Northern Boulevard Douglaston, NY 11363 Phone: (718) 631-0400, Monday, Wednesday, Friday 9 a